[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_k2xxw")
dialogue_id = "debate_magic_chemicals"
record_title = "Debate Speech: Magic Rituals"
text = "PAGE: historian(PORTAL_NETWORK), AUDIENCE
historian: Back when the priests among our ancestors practiced magical rituals, they settled a shard we now call The Fox Spirits Domain.
historian: When they first met these foxes, they considered them evil spirits, and poured circles of salt to ward them off.
historian: Over the centuries, that simple warding ritual became an obsession.
historian: In their zeal against spiritual impurity, they poisoned their soil and turned their landscape grey.
historian: They still hang on, surviving on hardy roots which are among the few plants that tolerate the harsh environment.
historian: When we try to enforce a holy order on nature, we risk destroying it.
historian: The real world is not a perfect temple designed for human purpose.
historian: It is a muddy, chaotic mess full of systems we don't understand.
historian: For one, we don't understand why the shards float the way they do, and until we learn that, trying to force them together at any cost is not a wise plan."
metadata/_custom_type_script = "uid://jtkfcsyiryo4"
